<main id="main">

<section class="tu-hero"><div class="tu-w tu-hero-g"><div><p class="tu-hand">hi! glad you&rsquo;re here &rarr;</p><h1>Make every tutoring hour count.</h1><p class="tu-lead">Tutored is an independent guide for students and parents. We explain how to pick a tutor, what a good session looks like and how to keep progress going between lessons, with small planning tools you can use tonight.</p><div class="tu-btns"><a class="tu-b" href="#quiz">Find your tutor type</a><a class="tu-b2" href="tutoring-session-guide.html">Read the session guide</a></div></div>
<div class="tu-board"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793486477835-a69a537e58ec?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=600&q=75" alt="two people working at a desk with papers and pens" width="560" height="600" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="tu-sticky"><b>Today&rsquo;s lesson plan</b><ol><li>Warm-up: 3 quick questions</li><li>Review last week&rsquo;s mistake</li><li>New idea, worked example</li><li>You try two on your own</li><li>Set one small goal</li></ol></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tu-s"><div class="tu-w"><p class="tu-hand tu-c">inside one good hour</p><h2 class="tu-c">A session, minute by minute</h2><div class="tu-clock"><div style="--w:8"><b>0&ndash;5</b><span>Warm-up</span><em>Settle in, recall last time</em></div><div style="--w:12"><b>5&ndash;15</b><span>Check homework</span><em>Find the stuck point</em></div><div style="--w:20"><b>15&ndash;35</b><span>Teach</span><em>One idea, explained clearly</em></div><div style="--w:15"><b>35&ndash;50</b><span>Practise</span><em>Student works, tutor watches</em></div><div style="--w:10"><b>50&ndash;60</b><span>Wrap up</span><em>Recap and next goal</em></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tu-s tu-lined" id="quiz"><div class="tu-w tu-quiz"><div class="tu-quiz-i"><p class="tu-hand">quick quiz</p><h2>What kind of tutor do you need?</h2><p>Four questions. No sign-up, nothing saved. Your answer appears below.</p></div><div class="tu-q" id="qz"><div class="tu-qp"><span id="qz-n">Question 1 of 4</span><i><b id="qz-bar"></b></i></div><div id="qz-q"></div><div class="tu-qo" id="qz-o"></div><div class="tu-qr" id="qz-r" aria-live="polite"></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tu-s"><div class="tu-w tu-cmp"><div><p class="tu-hand">honest comparison</p><h2>Tutor, class or self-study?</h2><p class="tu-lead">Each has a place. Many students do best mixing two of them.</p><figure class="tu-polar"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794209367402-1a560c057b94?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=300&q=75" alt="an instructor helping a child with climbing gear" width="420" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="tblw"><table class="tu-tbl"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Tutor</th><th>Class</th><th>Self-study</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Attention</th><td class="g">All on you</td><td class="m">Shared</td><td class="m">Your own</td></tr><tr><th>Pace</th><td class="g">Set to you</td><td class="b">Set by the group</td><td class="g">Set by you</td></tr><tr><th>Cost</th><td class="b">Highest</td><td class="m">Medium</td><td class="g">Lowest</td></tr><tr><th>Feedback</th><td class="g">Immediate</td><td class="m">Periodic</td><td class="b">Self-checked</td></tr><tr><th>Friends to learn with</th><td class="b">No</td><td class="g">Yes</td><td class="b">No</td></tr><tr><th>Best for</th><td>Gaps, exams, confidence</td><td>New material, routine</td><td>Revision, practice</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>

<section class="tu-s tu-ink"><div class="tu-w"><p class="tu-hand">a photo essay</p><h2>Learning by doing, with someone beside you</h2><div class="tu-essay"><figure class="e1"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794209166400-c3e2fed02d73?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="a man teaching three people to shape clay on pottery wheels" width="520" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>First, watch. A good tutor shows the whole movement once, slowly.</figcaption></figure><figure class="e2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794208936052-c2f5f204d03f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="hands of an adult and a child shaping a pot on a wheel" width="520" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Next, hands on. The student tries while the tutor stays close.</figcaption></figure><figure class="e3"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794209166834-69e8e68657f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="two people shaping wet clay on a pottery wheel" width="520" height="640" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Then, side by side. Over time the helper steps back and practice makes it stick.</figcaption></figure></div><blockquote class="tu-q2">&ldquo;Tell me and I forget. Teach me and I may remember. Involve me and I learn.&rdquo;<cite>Often attributed to Benjamin Franklin</cite></blockquote></div></section>

<section class="tu-s tu-lined"><div class="tu-w tu-chk"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1793486477903-38ee3f126ab9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=480&h=560&q=75" alt="two women working at a table with papers in a sunlit room" width="480" height="560" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="tu-hand">tick as you go</p><h2>Before the next session</h2><div class="tu-prog"><i><b id="ck-bar"></b></i><span id="ck-o">0 of 7 ready</span></div><ul class="tu-ck" id="ck"><li><label><input type="checkbox"> Homework finished, even if wrong</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> Marked the questions I got stuck on</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> Wrote down one thing I want to ask</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> Books, notes and calculator together</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> Looked at last session&rsquo;s notes</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> Quiet place, charged laptop if online</label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"> Know the date of my next test</label></li></ul></div></div></section>

<section class="tu-s" id="plan"><div class="tu-w"><p class="tu-hand tu-c">between lessons</p><h2 class="tu-c">Plan your week around the session</h2><div class="tu-pl-f"><label for="pl-d">Session day<select id="pl-d"><option>Mon</option><option>Tue</option><option selected>Wed</option><option>Thu</option><option>Fri</option><option>Sat</option><option>Sun</option></select></label><label for="pl-m">Practice minutes per day<select id="pl-m"><option>10</option><option selected>20</option><option>30</option><option>45</option></select></label></div><div class="tu-week" id="pl-w" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="tu-pl-n" id="pl-n"></p></div></section>

<section class="tu-s tu-yel"><div class="tu-w tu-signs"><div><p class="tu-hand">is it working?</p><h2>Six signs tutoring is paying off</h2></div><ul><li>Fewer &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t get it&rdquo; moments with homework</li><li>The student asks better, more specific questions</li><li>Mistakes repeat less from week to week</li><li>Test scores or teacher comments start to move</li><li>Less dread on the night before a lesson</li><li>They can explain an idea back in their own words</li></ul></div></section>

<section class="tu-s"><div class="tu-w tu-read"><a href="how-to-choose-a-tutor-guide.html"><small>guide one</small><b>How to Choose a Tutor</b><span>Qualifications, a trial lesson, the questions to ask and red flags to watch for.</span></a><a href="tutoring-session-guide.html"><small>guide two</small><b>The Tutoring Session</b><span>What happens in a good session, how to prepare and how to keep progress going after.</span></a></div></section>

